// markdownlint configuration for go-bricks.
//
// MD013 (line-length) is off deliberately. The repo writes long prose lines and
// wide tables by design — CLAUDE.md bullets routinely run past 400 characters
// because each one carries a full rationale. Measured against the tree, even a
// 200-character cap with code blocks and tables excluded still flagged 785
// hand-written prose lines, so any cap means reflowing prose for no reader
// benefit rather than catching a real defect.
//
// MD010 (no-hard-tabs) is scoped to prose. Go is tab-indented, so every Go
// sample in the wiki legitimately contains tabs; enforcing inside fenced blocks
// flagged 2,342 lines of correct example code.
//
// MD024 (no-duplicate-heading) is siblings_only because the wiki repeats
// section names like "Configuration" under different parents by design.
//
// MD038 (no-space-in-code) is off because its autofix is DESTRUCTIVE here, and
// not hypothetically: enabling it silently rewrote two documented literals in
// this repo. It stripped the trailing space from the mandated raw-SQL
// annotation prefix `// SECURITY: Manual SQL review completed - `, where the
// space is part of the prefix call sites are grepped against, and from the
// error string `unsupported database type: `, where the trailing space is what
// shows the empty %s interpolation — leaving that page contradicting its own
// before/after sample. The rule cannot distinguish whitespace that is content
// from whitespace that is a typo, and this repo documents literal strings
// constantly, so it is disabled rather than suppressed site by site.
{
  "config": {
    "MD013": false,
    "MD010": { "code_blocks": false },
    "MD024": { "siblings_only": true },
    "MD038": false
  },
  "globs": ["**/*.md"],
  // The globs above walk the filesystem, not git's index, so a checkout that has
  // accumulated ignored Markdown — agent reports, scratch plans, audit output —
  // fails `make check` on a tree git calls clean, while CI, which only ever checks
  // out tracked files, stays green. Deferring to .gitignore drops that scratch from
  // the walk. It does NOT reduce the set to exactly what CI sees: a doc written to
  // an allowlisted path (wiki/, docs/design/, ...) is untracked but not ignored, so
  // it is linted as soon as it exists — which is what a pre-commit gate should do.
  "gitignore": true,
  // Only paths git does NOT ignore belong here — `gitignore` above already covers
  // everything else, so node_modules, .claude/worktrees and plans were dropped as
  // dead entries when it was added.
  //
  // CHANGELOG.md is generated by release-please, so any fix applied here is
  // reverted by the next release and the gate breaks on a release PR nobody
  // hand-edits. Lint what humans write; the generator owns its own output.
  //
  // .claude/skills/improve is a tracked symlink whose target lives in the
  // gitignored .agents/ tree. `gitignore` above cannot exclude it: git tracks the
  // link itself, so the walked path is tracked while the files behind it are not.
  "ignores": ["CHANGELOG.md", ".claude/skills/improve"]
}
